      "writtenOn": "2022-12-20T01:33:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do you have timing measurements from your machine with the original version of this change (moving the mapAsync() earlier)? Knowing what sort of time cost this has would be helpful in prioritizing. Since the buffers are allocated in bulk and then used for many vertex/data writes, it could be that we can tune the allocation to amortize this?\n\nBut the equivalent of a submit or waitForFence sounds quite expensive; is there another lighter weight option that dawn could expose for this sort of synchronization? Primarily the hope would be not to introduce further complexity into the resource caching and returning timeline if possible, since all of that code has to be operatable on any thread (so it doesn\u0027t matter who un\u0027refs the last public Skia object).",
      "parentUuid": "947eba25_80c387a1",
